From: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:57:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-akita: Add the buttons

The Pixel 8a's volume and power keys are wired as on the Pixel 8 Pro:
volume down on gpa4-1, volume up on gpa6-2 and power on gpa4-0, all
active low and wake sources (Google's zuma-common.dtsi; the stock
phone's /proc/interrupts lists the same three gpio-keys lines). Add the
same gpio-keys node as zuma-husky, with zuma-pinctrl.dtsi's key pins.

Without it the power key is not an input device, so nothing on the
phone can wake the screen once the lock has blanked it.

Tested on a Pixel 8a from slot B (7.3.0-rc6): gpio-keys registers as an
input device with the three keys; one short press of each raises its
interrupt twice (press and release), and a short Power press wakes the
screen through the session's lock without powering the phone off.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts     | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
index 0f01727be..aad383858 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
 #include "zuma.dtsi"
 
 / {
@@ -77,6 +78,33 @@ framebuffer0: framebuffer {
 		};
 	};
 
+	gpio-keys {
+		compatible = "gpio-keys";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&key_voldown>, <&key_volup>, <&key_power>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		button-vol-down {
+			label = "KEY_VOLUMEDOWN";
+			linux,code = <KEY_VOLUMEDOWN>;
+			gpios = <&gpa4 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			wakeup-source;
+		};
+
+		button-vol-up {
+			label = "KEY_VOLUMEUP";
+			linux,code = <KEY_VOLUMEUP>;
+			gpios = <&gpa6 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			wakeup-source;
+		};
+
+		button-power {
+			label = "KEY_POWER";
+			linux,code = <KEY_POWER>;
+			gpios = <&gpa4 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			wakeup-source;
+		};
+	};
+
 	reserved-memory {
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
